# User-facing errors (Horus pattern)

Players must never see raw transport/debug text in Alerts, banners, or screens.

## Do not show in UI
- Timeout / HTTP status internals
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` env names
- Stack traces, `AbortError`, native exception text

## Do instead
- Log with `console.error` (and future Crashlytics)
- Use `toUserFacingMessage(error, fallback)` from `shared/lib/userFacingError`
- Keep `ApiError.message` as localized product copy only

```ts
// ❌ BAD
Alert.alert('Error', String(error))

// ✅ GOOD
Alert.alert(t('common.retry'), toUserFacingMessage(error, t('errors.catalogLoad')))
```

## Reference
Horus platform-app: map network/timeout/5xx → i18n; show API `message` only for deliberate domain errors.
